04:43:57.566 THIS CHANNEL ANSWERS PACKETS - the default since 2026-09-14. It used to need
04:43:57.566   --set-field-probe, a flag every caller passed and whose absence cost a launch;
04:43:57.566   --silent-channel is the way to turn answering off now, and it is only for
04:43:57.566   eliminating the channel as a variable.
04:43:57.566   This channel answers: the migration hello with a SetField
04:43:57.566   carrying the character's real record (presence[0] the stat block, presence[2]
04:43:57.566   the equipped list), 0x00DC with that field's NPCs and mobs, 0x00D1 with the
04:43:57.566   portal's destination, 0x00E7 with the !map GM command, and 0x0151 with a
04:43:57.566   script Say, 0x0104 with the NPC shop, and 0x00D2 with a channel migration.
04:43:57.566   CONFIRMED on a real client: the dressed character, the bag and its 125 slots,
04:43:57.566   NPC dialogue, mobs spawning and moving, an unequip that survives a map change.
04:43:57.566   NOT yet seen on screen: the shop counter, the quest journal, the channel
04:43:57.566   switch. Dropping an item is refused on purpose - there is nowhere to put it.
